==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/en|been}}, {{l/en|bene}}
* {{l/en|bien}} {{qualifier|Scotland}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|been|lang=enm}}, {{term|beene|lang=enm}}, {{term|bene||gracious, generous, pleasant|lang=enm}}, of unknown origin. Perhaps from {{etyl|non|en}} {{term|beinn||straight, right, favourable, advantageous, convenient, friendly, fair, keen|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|bainaz||straight|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bhei-||to hit, beat|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|bein|lang=sco}}, {{term|bien||in good condition, pleasant, well-to-do, cosy, well-stocked, pleasant, keen|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|beinn||straight, direct, hospitable|lang=is}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|bein||straight, direct, easy to deal with|lang=no}}. See also {{l/en|bain}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|dialectal|lang=en}} [[wealthy|Wealthy]]; [[well-to-do]].
#: ''a '''bein''' farmer''
# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|dialectal|lang=en}} Well provided; [[comfortable]]; [[cosy]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l/en|beinly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{context|Now|_|chiefly|dialectal|lang=en}} [[comfortably|Comfortably]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|Scotland|lang=en}} To [[render]] or make comfortable; [[dry]].

